  "environment_caveats": [
    "Audited the apex production domain https://crew3r.com. The client record still has no apex_cutover.completed_at key, but carries cut_over_at 2026-08-08 ('crew3r.com live 08-08'); the apex returned HTTP 200 on all six URLs and sends no x-robots-tag: noindex. Apex is the correct origin and the Step 4 staging SEO-exclusion correction does NOT apply. All four Lighthouse categories count toward the verdicts. Same origin as the 2026-08-26 baseline, so deltas are like-for-like.",
    "Lighthouse ran DESKTOP only (formFactor=desktop, cpuSlowdownMultiplier=1, throughputKbps=10240, rttMs=40). Mobile scores would typically land 10-20 performance points lower. Do not read these as mobile-first scores.",
    "Client record status is still 'onboarding', not 'active' (flagged in the August audit too). Proceeded because build_status is pushed_main and the apex is live and auditable.",
    "The named MCP tools on_page_lighthouse and on_page_instant_pages are not exposed by this DataForSEO MCP build. Used authenticated REST calls to /v3/on_page/lighthouse/live/json and /v3/on_page/instant_pages, piped to /tmp/rank-ai-audit/raw/ and parsed. Lighthouse live/json returns the full audit set (0.75-1.1 MB per URL), so failing-audit detail was captured without a separate full_data call. Spend: 6 x $0.005 + 6 x $0.00015 = about $0.03.",
    "has_micromarkup_errors cleared on all five URLs where it fired in August, which flips those pages amber to green. The rendered JSON-LD is unchanged in the relevant respect: the terminal BreadcrumbList ListItem still has no item property. DataForSEO also now reports has_micromarkup: false on every page even though each page ships 3-5 parseable JSON-LD blocks, so the vendor's micromarkup detection changed between runs rather than the site being fixed. The green verdicts are correct under the rubric but should not be read as the breadcrumb recommendation having been implemented.",
    "The August state stored only the top 5 Lighthouse issues per URL. New-issue detection therefore lists an audit as new only when it is high severity (it would have outranked the stored mediums) or when the prior list was complete (fewer than 5 items, i.e. the homepage). This run also stores all_failing_lighthouse_audit_ids per URL so October can diff the full set.",
    "LCP rose on every page (+47ms to +667ms) while scores stayed 97-100. Single-run desktop Lighthouse has run-to-run variance of roughly 100-300ms at these values, so only /contact/ (+667ms, FCP 290ms to 776ms) is a strong signal; / and /service-areas/brookings-sd/ crossed the 200ms flag threshold but should be confirmed on the next run before acting on them alone.",
    "DataForSEO 'frame' fires on /service-areas/brookings-sd/ again (one map <iframe>, no <frame>/<frameset>). Vendor false positive, not reported. no_image_title (image title attributes) and has_render_blocking_resources / high_loading_time are outside the Step 3 check list and are covered by Lighthouse; not double-counted."
  ],
